EXPERIMENT 17: Hierarchical Reinforcement Learning using HAM and MAXQ
Aim

To implement Hierarchical Reinforcement Learning (HRL) for an autonomous household robot to perform multiple tasks efficiently using HAM and MAXQ.

Algorithm / Procedure
Define high-level household tasks.
Divide each task into smaller subtasks.
Define states and actions for each subtask.
Use HAM to represent task hierarchy.
Use MAXQ to decompose the overall task into subtasks.
Assign rewards to completed subtasks.
Execute subtasks according to the hierarchy.
Calculate the total reward and task completion time.
Program
tasks = {
    "Clean": ["Move", "Pick", "Clean"],
    "Kitchen": ["Move", "Pick", "Place"],
    "Room": ["Move", "Pick", "Place"]
}


reward = {
    "Move": 1,
    "Pick": 2,
    "Clean": 5,
    "Place": 3
}


print("Hierarchical Robot Tasks:\n")


total_reward = 0


for task, subtasks in tasks.items():


    print(task, ":")


    for subtask in subtasks:
        print("  ->", subtask)
        total_reward += reward[subtask]


print("\nTotal Reward:", total_reward)
print("All Tasks Completed")
